# **Git Commands – Complete List for Lab & Exams 📚**

Here is a categorized list of important Git commands, from basic to advanced, with their syntax and purpose.

## **1. Git Configuration Commands**

| Command                                  | Purpose                |
| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |
| `git --version`                          | Check Git version      |
| `git config --global user.name "Name"`   | Set username           |
| `git config --global user.email "email"` | Set email              |
| `git config --list`                      | Display configurations |
| `git config --global --edit`             | Edit Git configuration |
| `git config --unset user.name`           | Remove a configuration |

## **2. Repository Creation Commands**

| Command                    | Purpose                                |
| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| `git init`                 | Initialize a new repository            |
| `git init project`         | Create a repository in a new folder    |
| `git clone URL`            | Copy remote repository to local system |
| `git clone URL foldername` | Clone into a specified folder          |

## **3. Basic Git Commands**

| Command                           | Purpose                                 |
| --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| `git status`                      | Check working directory status          |
| `git add filename`                | Add a particular file to staging        |
| `git add .`                       | Add all changes to staging              |
| `git add -A`                      | Stage all changes                       |
| `git commit -m "message"`         | Save staged changes                     |
| `git commit -am "message"`        | Stage and commit modified tracked files |
| `git log`                         | Display commit history                  |
| `git log --oneline`               | Display commits in one line             |
| `git log --oneline --all --graph` | Visualize branch history                |
| `git show`                        | Display details of a commit             |
| `git diff`                        | Show unstaged changes                   |
| `git diff --staged`               | Show staged changes                     |

## **4. File Management Commands**

| Command                         | Purpose                                        |
| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| `git rm filename`               | Delete a tracked file                          |
| `git rm --cached filename`      | Remove file from Git tracking but keep locally |
| `git mv old new`                | Rename or move a tracked file                  |
| `git restore filename`          | Discard unstaged changes                       |
| `git restore --staged filename` | Unstage a file                                 |
| `git clean -n`                  | Preview untracked files to delete              |
| `git clean -f`                  | Delete untracked files                         |

## **5. Git Branch Commands**

| Command                      | Purpose                            |
| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| `git branch`                 | List local branches                |
| `git branch branchname`      | Create a branch                    |
| `git branch -a`              | List all local and remote branches |
| `git branch -r`              | List remote branches               |
| `git switch branchname`      | Switch to a branch                 |
| `git switch -c branchname`   | Create and switch to a branch      |
| `git checkout branchname`    | Switch branches (older method)     |
| `git checkout -b branchname` | Create and switch branches         |
| `git branch -d branchname`   | Delete a merged branch             |
| `git branch -D branchname`   | Force-delete a branch              |
| `git branch -m newname`      | Rename current branch              |

## **6. Git Merge Commands**

| Command                | Purpose                                  |
| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `git merge branchname` | Merge another branch into current branch |
| `git merge --abort`    | Abort an ongoing merge                   |
| `git merge --continue` | Continue after resolving conflicts       |
| `git mergetool`        | Open merge conflict resolution tool      |

**Example:**

```
git switch main
git merge feature
```

This merges the feature branch into main.

